{
  "guidance": {
    "anti_examples": [
      "Using conflicts_with to express similarity (use `similar_to`)"
    ],
    "examples": [
      "core.Policy conflicts_with core.Policy (two rules cannot both hold for the same scope)"
    ],
    "sections": [
      "## Definition\n`X conflicts_with Y` means X and Y cannot both be satisfied/true in the same scope (a direct contradiction or incompatibility).\n\n## Notes\n- Keep semantics crisp.\n- Do not overload one relation with multiple meanings (Lucidity).\n\n## Use when\n- Two statements/constraints cannot both be satisfied in the same scope.\n\n## Do not use when\n- You mean tradeoff/choice history (track in decisions) or simple difference without contradiction.\n\n## Domain / Range\n- Domain: policies/constraints/invariants\n- Range: policies/constraints/invariants\n"
    ]
  },
  "ont": {
    "axis_default": "left",
    "characteristics": {
      "symmetric": true,
      "transitive": false
    },
    "description": "X steht im Konflikt/Widerspruch zu Y",
    "group": "opposition",
    "id": "core.rel.conflicts_with",
    "inverse": "core.rel.conflicts_with",
    "labels": [
      "conflicts_with"
    ],
    "type": "relation"
  },
  "schema": "rocs-source-experiment.v0",
  "system4d": null
}

{
  "guidance": {
    "anti_examples": [
      "Using depends_on for mere 'uses' relationships"
    ],
    "examples": [
      "core.Service depends_on core.IntegrationEdge (service needs an external integration)"
    ],
    "sections": [
      "## Definition\n`X depends_on Y` means X requires Y to function correctly (runtime/build/operational requirement).\n\n## Notes\n- Keep semantics crisp.\n- Do not overload one relation with multiple meanings (Lucidity).\n\n## Use when\n- X requires Y to function correctly (runtime, build, or operational requirement).\n\n## Do not use when\n- X just uses Y optionally or incidentally (use `uses`), or X is a part of Y (use `part_of`).\n\n## Domain / Range\n- Domain: any system element (`core.Service`, `core.Pipeline`, `core.Repo`)\n- Range: required element (`core.Service`, `core.IntegrationEdge`, `core.Policy`, etc)\n"
    ]
  },
  "ont": {
    "axis_default": "parents",
    "characteristics": {
      "symmetric": false,
      "transitive": false
    },
    "description": "X benötigt Y, um korrekt zu funktionieren",
    "group": "dependency",
    "id": "core.rel.depends_on",
    "labels": [
      "depends_on"
    ],
    "type": "relation"
  },
  "schema": "rocs-source-experiment.v0",
  "system4d": null
}

{
  "guidance": {
    "anti_examples": [
      "Using is_a for instances/values (use `instance_of`)"
    ],
    "examples": [
      "core.Agent is_a core.Actor"
    ],
    "sections": [
      "## Definition\n`X is_a Y` means X is a subtype of Y (inherits Y’s meaning/constraints); use for taxonomy only.\n\n## Notes\n- Keep semantics crisp.\n- Do not overload one relation with multiple meanings (Lucidity).\n\n## Use when\n- X is a subtype/specialization of Y (inherits meaning/constraints).\n\n## Do not use when\n- You mean instance/value membership (use `instance_of`) or part-whole (use `part_of`).\n\n## Domain / Range\n- Domain: subtype concept\n- Range: supertype concept\n"
    ]
  },
  "ont": {
    "axis_default": "parents",
